# React performance (extension UI)

Client-only React 18 popup/options — **not** Next.js/RSC. Full catalog:  
https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/react-best-practices  
Project skill: `.cursor/skills/react-best-practices/SKILL.md`

## Bundle

- Heavy/optional UI → `React.lazy` + `Suspense` (pattern: `OptionsPanel` lazy-loads options `App`).
- Do not eager-import Monaco or the options tree on the popup critical path.
- Prefer direct imports; avoid barrels that pull large modules.

## Async / storage

- Independent `browser.storage` / messaging reads → `Promise.all`.
- Defer awaits until the branch needs them; cheap sync guards first.
- Minimize and version persisted shapes (`src/shared/storage.ts`).

## Re-renders

- Derive values during render; do not mirror props into state via effects.
- Do **not** add `useMemo`/`useCallback` by default. Match existing App usage or fix a real issue; prefer splitting components to narrow subscriptions.
- Functional `setState` when next depends on previous; lazy `useState(() => …)` for expensive init.

## Skip (N/A here)

`server-*`, RSC/`React.cache`, `next/dynamic`, hydration-mismatch tricks — unless a rare case truly maps.
